From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: misc-de <misc-de@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 15:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] screen-saver-manager: Send the locked hint once logind is
 there

Phosh locks right at startup, before the login1 session proxy is ready,
so the change of the lockscreen manager's locked property found no proxy
and logind's LockedHint stayed false. The first unlock with the PIN then
changed nothing at logind, and services that follow LockedHint (here the
face unlock service) missed it. Send the current state once the proxy is
there.
---
 src/screen-saver-manager.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/screen-saver-manager.c b/src/screen-saver-manager.c
index 16031e19..63a8c6e6 100644
--- a/src/screen-saver-manager.c
+++ b/src/screen-saver-manager.c
@@ -675,6 +675,14 @@ on_logind_get_session_proxy_finish  (GObject                 *object,
     "swapped-object-signal::lock", G_CALLBACK (on_logind_lock), self,
     "swapped-object-signal::unlock", G_CALLBACK (on_logind_unlock), self,
     NULL);
+
+  /* The shell may have locked before the proxy was there (lock on startup):
+   * send the current state so logind's LockedHint matches */
+  phosh_dbus_login_session_call_set_locked_hint (self->logind_session_proxy,
+                                                 phosh_lockscreen_manager_get_locked (self->lockscreen_manager),
+                                                 self->cancel,
+                                                 on_locked_hint_set,
+                                                 NULL);
 }
 
 
